Fact Check-
We started our investigation by running a reverse image search on the same. The results led us to an extended version of the video posted by
IHA News
on its video report on 22 November 2024. The report states, "Israeli forces struck the Burj Shemali district, the town of Deir Mimas, the south of the capital Beirut, the Qotrani Town and the Deir Qanoun Ras Al-Ain Town in Lebanon. According to the Lebanese Ministry of Health, the attacks killed three health workers in the town of Qotrani and two health workers in the town of Deir Qanoun Ras Al-Ain and injured several more".
Using these hints, we conducted further searches and found a report by
The Guardian
published on 22 November, 2024. The report states, that it shows the moment an Israeli strike brought down a building in the Chiyah area of Beirut's southern suburbs on 22 November.
This makes it clear that the viral video is not a recent and it is not from Pakistan.
Conclusion-
Fact Crescendo found the claim made along with the viral video to be False. The video is old and depicts an Israeli strike that flattens a building in South Beirut, Lebanon.
